"""Glade grass: a bushy vegetative grass clump (GP roadmap, Phases 1, 2 and 4).

Structure and timing only (P5): which leaves and tillers exist, where they attach, and their age, size, angles
and state. Each Leaf and Tiller module carries `o`, a dict with exactly the organ-table fields of the roadmap's
format (G2, G15, G45), recomputed every step; the exporter (export_organs.py) copies them. The viewer draws a skeleton.

The track is the healthy plant (G15): a leaf's sizes, angle and arch are its healthy baseline at its age, while
senescence (turnover), fade (removal after a turnover death) and decline_draw carry the rest. Decline is a second
axis, the plant's vitality v (1 healthy, 0 gone), applied on top by decline.py (G10 to G14); the track never
contains it. A turnover leaf is senescent for SENESCENCE_DURATION, then dead, then fades over FADE_DURATION and is
collapsed at fade 1 (zero sizes, attach at its tiller base).

Open in the L-Py GUI:  ~/miniconda3/envs/lpy/bin/lpy cobeart-app/public/worlds/glade/dev/lpy/grass.lpy
then Run (whole derivation) or Animate (step by step); Rewind restarts from the seed. Parameters can be edited
in the block below (or in the GUI's parameter panel, since they are externs).

Decline preview (G17): the derivation runs to T_END + PREVIEW_DECLINE. After T_END the productions freeze (every
module is reproduced unchanged) and the viewer draws the frozen plant at v = 1 - (t - T_END) / PREVIEW_DECLINE:
leaves and sheaths brown, droop and shrivel by their health, tillers lean outward, and everything fades once
v < V_DEAD. So Run with the defaults ends on an empty scene (fully faded at T_END + PREVIEW_DECLINE): use Animate
to watch growth and decline, or set PREVIEW_DECLINE to 0 to Run to the grown plant. Lower T_END to preview decline
from a younger plant. The exporter samples only up to T_END.

Units: metres and radians, Z up. Time is in phyllochrons (P, the interval between two leaves on the main shoot);
one derivation step advances time by DT. A leaf of rank r on the main shoot is born at t = r - 1. Tillers emerge a
little after their trigger and keep their own phyllochron (G20), so shoots do not grow or drop leaves in step.

A leaf's azimuth_rad and angle_from_axis_rad are spherical angles in its tiller's frame: the pole is the tiller
direction and the frame is the minimal rotation taking +Z onto it (identity for the main shoot). direction is that
rotation applied to those angles, in world space, and is the authoritative field.

A leaf's senescence_duration (its birth draw, see SENESCENCE_JITTER) is in `o` too (G45): once a leaf turns
senescent its senescence rises by DT / senescence_duration per step, so the exporter can write its event times and a
consumer can rebuild senescence and fade in closed form (G38).

Use one Lsystem instance, derived forward only; birth draws live in module globals reset by Start(). Everything
that changes after birth (age, state, senescence, fade) is carried in the modules.

Parameters (all externs, overridable with Lsystem(path, {"NAME": value})):
  SEED                     seed of the random streams; every organ draws once, at its birth
  DT                       time step in P
  T_END                    end time in P of the growth track (what the exporter samples)
  LIVE_LEAVES              live (growing or mature) leaves per tiller before the oldest senesces (P7)
  MAX_TILLERS              first-order tillers, from the axils of main-shoot leaves 1..MAX_TILLERS (P1, P7)
  TILLER_DELAY             the bud in main-shoot leaf n's axil is triggered when leaf n + TILLER_DELAY appears
  TILLER_EMERGENCE_JITTER  a tiller emerges a uniform [0, J] P after its trigger (own stream per tiller, G20)
  TILLER_PHYLLOCHRON_JITTER  a tiller's phyllochron is 1 + uniform(-J, J) P; the main shoot's is 1 (G20)
  TILLER_SIZE_SCALE        size factor on every tiller leaf relative to the main shoot's progression
  CROWN_RADIUS_M           distance of a tiller's base from the crown centre
  TILLER_SPLAY_DEG         outward tilt of a tiller's axis from vertical, with TILLER_SPLAY_JITTER_DEG
  TILLER_AZIMUTH_SPREAD_DEG  a tiller's azimuth is its parent leaf's azimuth turned by this angle (plus
                           uniform TILLER_AZIMUTH_SPREAD_JITTER_DEG), so the clump becomes radial instead of a
                           vertical fan (same-side tiller bases crowd and push apart, Tokuyama et al. 2021). The
                           turn direction alternates between successive tillers on the same side of the main shoot:
                           side occurrence (parent_rank - 1) // 2 even turns +, odd turns -, so with 4 tillers
                           tillers 1 and 3 turn opposite ways, likewise 2 and 4. The tiller's base, splay and leaf
                           plane (first leaf faces the tiller azimuth, alternating from there) follow this azimuth.
  BASE_AZIMUTH_RAD         azimuth of the main shoot's first leaf
  AZIMUTH_JITTER_RAD       per-leaf jitter on the alternating (distichous) azimuth
  RANK_PLATEAU             rank at which the size progressions stop growing
  SHEATH_RANK1_M, SHEATH_PLATEAU_M, SHEATH_JITTER        sheath length at rank 1, at the plateau, relative jitter
  BLADE_RANK1_M, BLADE_PLATEAU_M, BLADE_JITTER           blade length likewise
  WIDTH_RANK1_M, WIDTH_PLATEAU_M, WIDTH_JITTER           blade width likewise
  ELONGATION_AGE           age (P) at which sheath, blade and width reach full size (smoothstep from 0)
  MATURE_AGE               age at which the collar appears and the leaf turns mature
  UNROLL_START_AGE, UNROLL_DURATION   unroll fraction is smoothstep((age - start) / duration)
  ANGLE_YOUNG_DEG, ANGLE_MATURE_DEG, ANGLE_OLD_DEG       angle from the tiller axis: young and rolled, at
                                                         maturity, and eased toward after maturity
  ANGLE_SPREAD_DURATION    time after maturity over which the angle eases to ANGLE_OLD_DEG
  ANGLE_JITTER_DEG         per-leaf jitter on the angle from the tiller axis
  ARCH_YOUNG_RAD, ARCH_OLD_RAD, ARCH_AGE   arch (bend) rises from young to old over ARCH_AGE
  SENESCENCE_DURATION      time from turning senescent to dead (turnover)
  SENESCENCE_JITTER        a leaf's turnover senescence lasts SENESCENCE_DURATION * (1 + uniform(-J, J)) (G20)
  FADE_DURATION            time from a turnover leaf's death to its full fade (then it is collapsed)
  PREVIEW_DECLINE          length (P) of the decline preview after T_END; 0 turns it off
  Look and decline (applied through decline.py, whose DeclineParams uses these names):
  ANGLE_SENESCENT_DEG      extra angle from the tiller axis at health 0
  SHRIVEL_FRACTION         final fraction of health over which a leaf shrivels to DECLINE_RESIDUAL and droops
                           (1: gradually over the whole decline, from health 1 to 0)
  SHRIVEL_ANGLE_DEG, SHRIVEL_ARCH_RAD      extra angle and arch reached at the end of the shrivel
  DECLINE_RESIDUAL         size of a dead leaf relative to its healthy size
  V_DEAD                   vitality at which every leaf is dead; below it the plant fades and cannot revive
  DECLINE_AGE_SPREAD, DECLINE_AGE_REF      older leaves die earlier in v, by up to the spread at age AGE_REF
  DECLINE_JITTER           scale of a leaf's unit decline_draw (uniform in [-1, 1], drawn at birth) on its death point
  DECLINE_SPLAY_DEG        outward lean of every tiller but the main shoot, reached at V_DEAD
"""
import importlib
import math
import os
import random
import sys

from openalea.plantgl.all import Index3, TriangleSet, Vector3

# L-Py does not put the model's folder on the import path; __file__ is the .lpy path L-Py sets.
_MODEL_DIR = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
if _MODEL_DIR not in sys.path:
    sys.path.insert(0, _MODEL_DIR)
import decline  # noqa: E402
importlib.reload(decline)  # a GUI reload of the model picks up edits to decline.py
from decline import cross, dir_from, rotate, to_tiller_frame, unit  # noqa: E402

extern(
    SEED = 1,
    DT = 0.05,
    T_END = 12.0,
    LIVE_LEAVES = 3,
    MAX_TILLERS = 4,
    TILLER_DELAY = 3,
    TILLER_EMERGENCE_JITTER = 0.6,
    TILLER_PHYLLOCHRON_JITTER = 0.15,
    TILLER_SIZE_SCALE = 0.9,
    CROWN_RADIUS_M = 0.004,
    TILLER_SPLAY_DEG = 12.0,
    TILLER_SPLAY_JITTER_DEG = 4.0,
    TILLER_AZIMUTH_SPREAD_DEG = 50.0,
    TILLER_AZIMUTH_SPREAD_JITTER_DEG = 15.0,
    BASE_AZIMUTH_RAD = 0.4,
    AZIMUTH_JITTER_RAD = 0.45,
    RANK_PLATEAU = 5,
    SHEATH_RANK1_M = 0.02,
    SHEATH_PLATEAU_M = 0.08,
    SHEATH_JITTER = 0.15,
    BLADE_RANK1_M = 0.06,
    BLADE_PLATEAU_M = 0.20,
    BLADE_JITTER = 0.10,
    WIDTH_RANK1_M = 0.004,
    WIDTH_PLATEAU_M = 0.013,
    WIDTH_JITTER = 0.08,
    ELONGATION_AGE = 2.0,
    MATURE_AGE = 2.0,
    UNROLL_START_AGE = 0.6,
    UNROLL_DURATION = 1.2,
    ANGLE_YOUNG_DEG = 8.0,
    ANGLE_MATURE_DEG = 20.0,
    ANGLE_OLD_DEG = 48.0,
    ANGLE_SPREAD_DURATION = 1.0,
    ANGLE_JITTER_DEG = 5.0,
    ANGLE_SENESCENT_DEG = 12.0,
    ARCH_YOUNG_RAD = 0.4,
    ARCH_OLD_RAD = 0.9,
    ARCH_AGE = 3.0,
    SENESCENCE_DURATION = 2.0,
    SENESCENCE_JITTER = 0.2,
    SHRIVEL_FRACTION = 1.0,
    SHRIVEL_ANGLE_DEG = 25.0,
    SHRIVEL_ARCH_RAD = 0.8,
    FADE_DURATION = 0.5,
    PREVIEW_DECLINE = 6.0,
    DECLINE_RESIDUAL = 0.7,
    V_DEAD = 0.15,
    DECLINE_AGE_SPREAD = 0.4,
    DECLINE_AGE_REF = 3.0,
    DECLINE_JITTER = 0.1,
    DECLINE_SPLAY_DEG = 25.0,
)

PHYLLOCHRON = 1.0  # time is measured in main-shoot phyllochrons, so its interval between two leaves is 1
UP = (0.0, 0.0, 1.0)
EPS = 1e-9
for _name in ("DT", "SENESCENCE_DURATION", "FADE_DURATION"):
    if not globals()[_name] > 0:
        raise ValueError("%s must be positive, got %r" % (_name, globals()[_name]))
for _name in ("TILLER_EMERGENCE_JITTER", "TILLER_PHYLLOCHRON_JITTER", "SENESCENCE_JITTER"):
    if not globals()[_name] >= 0:
        raise ValueError("%s must be >= 0, got %r" % (_name, globals()[_name]))
for _name in ("TILLER_PHYLLOCHRON_JITTER", "SENESCENCE_JITTER"):
    if not globals()[_name] < 1:
        raise ValueError("%s must be < 1 so every duration stays positive, got %r" % (_name, globals()[_name]))
DECLINE = decline.DeclineParams.from_mapping(globals())


def smoothstep(x):
    x = min(max(x, 0.0), 1.0)
    return x * x * (3.0 - 2.0 * x)


def lerp(a, b, f):
    return a + (b - a) * f


def rank_value(rank, at_rank1, at_plateau):
    """Linear from rank 1 to RANK_PLATEAU, flat after."""
    return lerp(at_rank1, at_plateau, min(max((rank - 1) / (RANK_PLATEAU - 1), 0.0), 1.0))


def jitter(rel):
    return 1.0 + RNG.uniform(-rel, rel)


# Birth state outside the L-string, fixed once drawn. Reset in Start() so a GUI rewind replays the same plant.
RNG = random.Random(SEED)
TILLER_O = {}     # tiller id -> its organ fields (fixed at birth)
LEAF_DRAWS = {}   # leaf id -> random draws and birth time, fixed at birth
TILLER_DRAWS = {}  # tiller id -> emergence delay and phyllochron, drawn once from the tiller's own streams
NEWEST_RANK = {}  # tiller id -> rank of its newest leaf once this step's emissions are done (see EndEach)
STATE_TIME = 0.0  # time of the current L-string, read by the decline preview (set in EndEach)


def reset():
    global RNG, STATE_TIME
    RNG = random.Random(SEED)
    STATE_TIME = 0.0
    TILLER_O.clear()
    LEAF_DRAWS.clear()
    TILLER_DRAWS.clear()
    NEWEST_RANK.clear()
    TILLER_O[0] = {"base": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "direction": list(UP), "azimuth_rad": BASE_AZIMUTH_RAD,
                   "splay_rad": 0.0}


reset()  # the axiom reads TILLER_O[0] before Start runs


def Start():
    reset()


def emits(t_next):
    """Whether an Apex with this countdown emits a leaf in the current step."""
    return t_next < DT / 2


def EndEach(lstring):
    """Record the time of the new L-string and, per tiller, the newest leaf rank after the next step's emissions.

    Leaves and buds read the ranks in the next step, so a leaf turns senescent in the same step as the leaf that
    would make its tiller exceed LIVE_LEAVES, and a bud activates in the same step as its triggering leaf.
    """
    global STATE_TIME
    STATE_TIME = (getIterationNb() + 1) * DT  # getIterationNb() is the index of the step just done
    NEWEST_RANK.clear()
    for m in lstring:
        if m.name == "Apex":
            tiller, rank, t_next = m[0], m[1], m[2]
            NEWEST_RANK[tiller] = rank if emits(t_next) else rank - 1


def now():
    """Time of the state the current production step reads."""
    return getIterationNb() * DT


def frozen():
    """Whether the current step lies in the decline preview after T_END, where every module stays unchanged."""
    return now() >= T_END - DT / 2


def preview_vitality():
    """Vitality v of the current L-string in the decline preview (1 up to T_END)."""
    if PREVIEW_DECLINE <= 0:
        return 1.0
    return min(max(1.0 - (STATE_TIME - T_END) / PREVIEW_DECLINE, 0.0), 1.0)


def leaf_id(tiller, rank):
    return "L%d.%d" % (tiller, rank)


def tiller_draws(tiller):
    """A tiller's emergence delay and phyllochron (G20), each from its own seeded stream, so RNG is untouched."""
    if tiller not in TILLER_DRAWS:
        if tiller == 0:
            TILLER_DRAWS[0] = {"emergence_delay": 0.0, "phyllochron": PHYLLOCHRON}
        else:
            TILLER_DRAWS[tiller] = {
                "emergence_delay": random.Random("emergence:%d:T%d" % (SEED, tiller)).uniform(
                    0.0, TILLER_EMERGENCE_JITTER),
                "phyllochron": PHYLLOCHRON * (1.0 + random.Random("phyllochron:%d:T%d" % (SEED, tiller)).uniform(
                    -TILLER_PHYLLOCHRON_JITTER, TILLER_PHYLLOCHRON_JITTER)),
            }
    return TILLER_DRAWS[tiller]


def trigger_time(rank):
    """Birth time of the main-shoot leaf that triggers the bud in leaf rank's axil, or None while it is unborn.

    In the step the trigger leaf appears, the bud's production runs before the main Apex's (buds sit left of it in
    the string), so the leaf is not drawn yet and NEWEST_RANK tells that it appears now.
    """
    trigger = LEAF_DRAWS.get(leaf_id(0, rank + TILLER_DELAY))
    if trigger is not None:
        return trigger["birth_time"]
    return now() if NEWEST_RANK.get(0, 0) >= rank + TILLER_DELAY else None


def bud_emerges(rank):
    """Whether the bud in main-shoot leaf rank's axil becomes a tiller in this step (trigger plus its delay)."""
    t = trigger_time(rank)
    return t is not None and now() >= t + tiller_draws(rank)["emergence_delay"] - DT / 2


def new_leaf(tiller, rank):
    """Draw a new leaf's randomness and return its first Leaf parameters (age DT after this step)."""
    tiller_az = TILLER_O[tiller]["azimuth_rad"]
    scale = TILLER_SIZE_SCALE if tiller > 0 else 1.0
    lid = leaf_id(tiller, rank)
    LEAF_DRAWS[lid] = {
        "azimuth_rad": math.remainder(tiller_az + (rank - 1) * math.pi
                                      + RNG.uniform(-AZIMUTH_JITTER_RAD, AZIMUTH_JITTER_RAD), 2 * math.pi),
        "angle_jitter_rad": math.radians(RNG.uniform(-ANGLE_JITTER_DEG, ANGLE_JITTER_DEG)),
        "sheath_m": rank_value(rank, SHEATH_RANK1_M, SHEATH_PLATEAU_M) * scale * jitter(SHEATH_JITTER),
        "blade_m": rank_value(rank, BLADE_RANK1_M, BLADE_PLATEAU_M) * scale * jitter(BLADE_JITTER),
        "width_m": rank_value(rank, WIDTH_RANK1_M, WIDTH_PLATEAU_M) * scale * jitter(WIDTH_JITTER),
        # Own streams per leaf, seeded from SEED and the id, so adding them left every draw of RNG unchanged.
        "decline_draw": random.Random("decline:%d:%s" % (SEED, lid)).uniform(-1.0, 1.0),
        "senescence_duration": SENESCENCE_DURATION * (1.0 + random.Random("senescence:%d:%s" % (SEED, lid)).uniform(
            -SENESCENCE_JITTER, SENESCENCE_JITTER)),
        "birth_time": now(),
    }
    return lid, now(), DT, "growing", leaf_o(lid, tiller, DT, "growing", 0.0, 0.0)


def new_tiller(tiller, parent_rank):
    """A first-order tiller on the crown, turned off its parent leaf's azimuth, splayed outward."""
    sign = 1.0 if ((parent_rank - 1) // 2) % 2 == 0 else -1.0  # alternate between same-side tillers
    spread = math.radians(TILLER_AZIMUTH_SPREAD_DEG + RNG.uniform(-TILLER_AZIMUTH_SPREAD_JITTER_DEG,
                                                                  TILLER_AZIMUTH_SPREAD_JITTER_DEG))
    az = math.remainder(LEAF_DRAWS[leaf_id(0, parent_rank)]["azimuth_rad"] + sign * spread, 2 * math.pi)
    splay = math.radians(TILLER_SPLAY_DEG + RNG.uniform(-TILLER_SPLAY_JITTER_DEG, TILLER_SPLAY_JITTER_DEG))
    o = {"base": [CROWN_RADIUS_M * math.cos(az), CROWN_RADIUS_M * math.sin(az), 0.0],
         "direction": dir_from(az, splay), "azimuth_rad": az, "splay_rad": splay}
    TILLER_O[tiller] = o
    return o


def leaf_o(lid, tiller, age, state, sen, fade):
    """Organ-table leaf fields: the healthy baseline at this age plus senescence and fade (pure given the draws)."""
    d = LEAF_DRAWS[lid]
    t = TILLER_O[tiller]
    size = 0.0 if fade >= 1.0 else smoothstep(age / ELONGATION_AGE)
    angle_deg = (ANGLE_YOUNG_DEG
                 + (ANGLE_MATURE_DEG - ANGLE_YOUNG_DEG) * smoothstep(age / MATURE_AGE)
                 + (ANGLE_OLD_DEG - ANGLE_MATURE_DEG) * smoothstep((age - MATURE_AGE) / ANGLE_SPREAD_DURATION))
    angle = max(math.radians(angle_deg) + d["angle_jitter_rad"], 0.0)
    sheath = d["sheath_m"] * size
    base, axis = t["base"], t["direction"]
    return {
        "attach": [base[i] + axis[i] * sheath for i in range(3)],
        "direction": unit(to_tiller_frame(dir_from(d["azimuth_rad"], angle), axis)),
        "azimuth_rad": d["azimuth_rad"],
        "angle_from_axis_rad": angle,
        "sheath_length_m": sheath,
        "blade_length_m": d["blade_m"] * size,
        "blade_width_m": d["width_m"] * size,
        "unroll": smoothstep((age - UNROLL_START_AGE) / UNROLL_DURATION),
        "arch_rad": lerp(ARCH_YOUNG_RAD, ARCH_OLD_RAD, smoothstep(age / ARCH_AGE)),
        "senescence": sen,
        "fade": fade,
        "decline_draw": d["decline_draw"],
        "senescence_duration": d["senescence_duration"],
    }


def next_state(lid, tiller, rank, age, state, sen, fade):
    """Leaf life cycle growing -> mature -> senescent (turnover) -> dead -> faded; returns state, senescence, fade."""
    if state in ("growing", "mature") and NEWEST_RANK.get(tiller, rank) - rank < LIVE_LEAVES:
        return ("mature" if age >= MATURE_AGE - EPS else "growing"), 0.0, 0.0
    if state != "dead":  # turning senescent this step (sen is 0) or already senescent
        sen = min(sen + DT / LEAF_DRAWS[lid]["senescence_duration"], 1.0)
        return ("dead", 1.0, 0.0) if sen >= 1.0 - EPS else ("senescent", sen, 0.0)
    fade = min(fade + DT / FADE_DURATION, 1.0)
    return "dead", 1.0, (1.0 if fade >= 1.0 - EPS else fade)


# Skeleton preview: world-space triangle meshes inserted with @g while the turtle stays unrotated at the origin.
# Materials form a grid of opacity levels (N_OPACITY) by colour slots: N_COLOURS browning steps of the blade
# (GREEN to BROWN), then N_COLOURS of the sheath (SHEATH_GREEN to BROWN), so the sheath browns with its leaf and
# fades show as transparency.
N_COLOURS, N_OPACITY = 12, 6
GREEN, BROWN, SHEATH_GREEN = (40, 120, 20), (140, 100, 45), (90, 120, 40)
COLOUR_BASE = 10
N_SLOTS = 2 * N_COLOURS
for _o in range(N_OPACITY):
    for _i in range(N_SLOTS):
        _green = GREEN if _i < N_COLOURS else SHEATH_GREEN
        _f = (_i % N_COLOURS) / (N_COLOURS - 1)
        context().turtle.setMaterial(COLOUR_BASE + _o * N_SLOTS + _i,
                                     Material(tuple(int(lerp(g, b, _f)) for g, b in zip(_green, BROWN)),
                                              transparency=1.0 - (_o + 1) / N_OPACITY))
BLADE_SEGMENTS, TUBE_SIDES = 8, 6
ROLLED_WIDTH = 0.25  # drawn width fraction of a fully rolled blade
MIN_DRAWN_OPACITY = 0.5 / N_OPACITY  # below this a leaf is not drawn


def material_index(browning, alpha, sheath):
    """Material of a blade or sheath at this browning, at the nearest non-zero opacity level."""
    level = min(max(int(math.ceil(alpha * N_OPACITY)) - 1, 0), N_OPACITY - 1)
    slot = int(round(browning * (N_COLOURS - 1))) + (N_COLOURS if sheath else 0)
    return COLOUR_BASE + level * N_SLOTS + slot


def drawn_leaf(tiller, age, o, v):
    """The leaf as drawn at vitality v (decline.declined_leaf on its track fields)."""
    return decline.declined_leaf(dict(o, age=age, tiller=tiller), TILLER_O[tiller], v, DECLINE)


def sheath_mesh(base, axis, length, radius):
    side = unit(cross(axis, [1.0, 0.0, 0.0] if abs(axis[0]) < 0.9 else [0.0, 1.0, 0.0]))
    other = cross(axis, side)
    pts = []
    for z in (0.0, length):
        for j in range(TUBE_SIDES):
            a = 2 * math.pi * j / TUBE_SIDES
            pts.append(Vector3(*[base[i] + axis[i] * z + radius * (math.cos(a) * side[i] + math.sin(a) * other[i])
                                 for i in range(3)]))
    idx = []
    for j in range(TUBE_SIDES):
        k = (j + 1) % TUBE_SIDES
        idx += [Index3(j, k, TUBE_SIDES + k), Index3(j, TUBE_SIDES + k, TUBE_SIDES + j)]
    return TriangleSet(pts, idx)


def blade_mesh(dl, azimuth, unroll):
    """Flat tapered strip from the collar, bending away from the tiller axis by arch_rad, narrower while rolled."""
    d = list(dl.direction)
    side = to_tiller_frame([-math.sin(azimuth), math.cos(azimuth), 0.0], dl.tiller_axis)  # axis-to-leaf plane normal
    step = dl.blade_length_m / BLADE_SEGMENTS
    width = dl.blade_width_m * lerp(ROLLED_WIDTH, 1.0, unroll)
    p, pts = list(dl.attach), []
    for i in range(BLADE_SEGMENTS + 1):
        s = i / BLADE_SEGMENTS
        half = 0.5 * width * min(1.0, 0.5 + 1.6 * s) * (1 - s) ** 0.6
        pts += [Vector3(*[p[k] - side[k] * half for k in range(3)]), Vector3(*[p[k] + side[k] * half for k in range(3)])]
        bent = rotate(d, side, dl.arch_rad * s * s)
        p = [p[k] + bent[k] * step for k in range(3)]
    idx = []
    for i in range(BLADE_SEGMENTS):
        a = 2 * i
        idx += [Index3(a, a + 1, a + 3), Index3(a, a + 3, a + 2)]
    return TriangleSet(pts, idx)


module Apex(tiller, rank, t_next), Leaf(id, tiller, rank, birth_time, age, state, o)
module Tiller(tiller, parent_rank, birth_time, o), Bud(tiller, rank, age)

Axiom: Tiller(0, 0, 0.0, TILLER_O[0]) Apex(0, 1, 0.0)

derivation length: int(round((T_END + PREVIEW_DECLINE) / DT))

production:

Apex(tiller, rank, t_next):
    if frozen():
        produce Apex(tiller, rank, t_next)
    if emits(t_next):
        lid, birth, age, state, o = new_leaf(tiller, rank)
        if tiller == 0 and rank <= MAX_TILLERS:
            produce Leaf(lid, tiller, rank, birth, age, state, o) Bud(tiller, rank, 0.0) Apex(tiller, rank + 1, t_next + tiller_draws(tiller)["phyllochron"] - DT)
        produce Leaf(lid, tiller, rank, birth, age, state, o) Apex(tiller, rank + 1, t_next + tiller_draws(tiller)["phyllochron"] - DT)
    produce Apex(tiller, rank, t_next - DT)

Bud(tiller, rank, age):
    if frozen():
        produce Bud(tiller, rank, age)
    if bud_emerges(rank):
        o = new_tiller(rank, rank)
        lid, birth, leaf_age, state, leaf = new_leaf(rank, 1)
        produce Tiller(rank, rank, now(), o) Leaf(lid, rank, 1, birth, leaf_age, state, leaf) Apex(rank, 2, tiller_draws(rank)["phyllochron"] - DT)
    produce Bud(tiller, rank, age + DT)

Leaf(lid, tiller, rank, birth, age, state, o):
    if frozen():
        produce Leaf(lid, tiller, rank, birth, age, state, o)
    new_age = age + DT
    new_state, sen, fade = next_state(lid, tiller, rank, new_age, state, o["senescence"], o["fade"])
    produce Leaf(lid, tiller, rank, birth, new_age, new_state, leaf_o(lid, tiller, new_age, new_state, sen, fade))

interpretation:

Tiller(tiller, parent_rank, birth_time, o) --> @M(0, 0, 0)
Leaf(lid, tiller, rank, birth, age, state, o):
    dl = drawn_leaf(tiller, age, o, preview_vitality())
    if dl.opacity < MIN_DRAWN_OPACITY:
        produce @M(0, 0, 0)
    radius = 0.25 * dl.blade_width_m + 0.0004
    produce @M(0, 0, 0) ,(material_index(dl.browning, dl.opacity, True)) @g(sheath_mesh(TILLER_O[tiller]["base"], dl.tiller_axis, dl.sheath_length_m, radius)) ,(material_index(dl.browning, dl.opacity, False)) @g(blade_mesh(dl, o["azimuth_rad"], o["unroll"]))
Apex(tiller, rank, t_next) --> @M(0, 0, 0)
Bud(tiller, rank, age) --> @M(0, 0, 0)

endlsystem
